317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 62 0 R
/T (Answer: A CNN normally contains convolutional layers, activation functions, pooling layers, flattening, fully connected layers, and an output layer. Convolutional layers extract image features, pooling reduces feature dimensions, and fully connected layers perform classification.)
/E (Answer: A CNN normally contains convolutional layers, activation functions, pooling layers, flattening, fully connected layers, and an output layer. Convolutional layers extract image features, pooling reduces feature dimensions, and fully connected layers perform classification.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 62 0 R
/T (Q3. What is the role of Convolutional Layers, Pooling Layers, and Fully Connected Layers in a CNN?)
